course: dictionary
lesson: 8698
title: Seller and buyer
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A seller is a person or shop that sells things for money. The opposite is a buyer, the person who buys. Every sale needs both: a seller who sells and a buyer who pays.
explain: Seller ends in -er, like teacher or runner. It means someone who does the action of selling. Sellers, with an s, means more than one.
explain: A best seller is a book or thing that very many people buy. A good seller is a thing that sells well. So seller can mean a person, a shop, or even a thing.
fact: A seller is a person or shop that sells things for money.
fact: A buyer is the opposite: the person who buys.
fact: «Market sellers often say a rounded price out loud, so it is worth doing the sum yourself.»
fact: A best seller is a book or thing that very many people buy.
fact: A good seller is a thing that sells well.
exercise: What is a seller? | A person who buys things at the market | A kind of coin | A long, boring story | *A person or shop that sells things for money
exercise: What is the opposite of a seller? | A shop | A bargain | *A buyer | A ticket
exercise: A book that very many people buy is called a what? | A library book | A bookmark | *A best seller | A slow reader
test: Which of these is a seller? | A reader in the library | A player in a football game | *A flower seller in the street | A bird in the park
test: Which phrase means a thing that sells well? | A slow reader | A bad buyer | A rounded price | *A good seller
exam: A fruit seller starts with 20 apples and sells 12 of them. How many apples are left? | 32 | 12 | 6 | *8
